Z||000032||StuGood||08-27-2000||02:39 PM||||Mark me down for two red Fieros - a 1986 SE (V6+auto), and a 1988 (L4+ 5-speed).  Sorry, have no pictures, but thought I'd add mine to the count.<P>I'm not particularly partial to red - but these two <B>are</B> the most inexpensive Fieros I ever bought.  Since I intend to sell the SE, I'm <B>glad</B> it's red - just about everyone I talk to seems to really <B>like</B> red sports cars  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  <P>There's nothing wrong with red - it's just not my personal favorite.  You guys <B>do</B>, however, have some fantastic looking cars here!  Nice work!    ||||reg||1
Z||000033||RossT||08-27-2000||02:47 PM||||Baldlobo,<BR>  you are correct!! I know what you go thru..  You can always tell the cars from North Dakota vs the cars from Mannitoba.  The ones from ND only have ONE electrical plug on the front of the car for engine block heater.  On the other hand cars from Mannitoba have FOUR electrical plugs on the front of the car.  One as an engine block heater, one as an oil heater, and one as a battery heater, and one as an in car heater.<BR>Man do you guys go thru the electricity in the winter,<P>AL, For the most part ND does not use salt in the winter. You can always tell the cars that have driven thru MN, for they are normally covered in salt. Cars tend not to rust like they do from Mn, Iowa or Wi.||||reg||1
